<p>British Prime Minister Keir Starmer faced a deepening challenge from within the governing Labour Party after Health Secretary Wes Streeting resigned on May 14, saying he had lost confidence in Starmer’s leadership and calling for a broad contest over the party’s future. The revolt followed heavy Labour losses in local and regional elections, with lawmakers questioning Starmer’s judgment less than two years after he led Labour back to power in July 2024 after 14 years in opposition. Streeting did not immediately launch a formal leadership bid, leaving Starmer’s critics to test whether a challenger could assemble enough parliamentary backing under Labour’s rules. Greater Manchester Mayor Andy Burnham won Labour National Executive Committee permission to seek selection for the Makerfield by-election, giving him a possible route to the Commons before any leadership bid. Reform UK leader Nigel Farage said his party would “throw absolutely everything” at the Makerfield contest, where Reform has gained ground after Labour’s local election defeats.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/iFkpfwg8MXoqKr5u8CboRYgMNfZF5XeRytnNQcuknz7WTssZCO8ex0JS5tVekJaUenXJksT2pXN23WePd1cPWTVBkPgoledPR4I8Lbs8MmfFUlruEJTknKnnsyxBaNmDthf1VEfs-ZaCQWjzKsRNGpwdFD1EWuOtPZF0RZ3Z63sVbziuNPS_vHNvrMcFGOh2J44jYcHUQUH0FfRktowfsS16ixisZ-_u0Tqk9Z65yMSK4KCSUAzhvwzIAFSnxmreOOpIj52H6r87tjfSsg' alt='British Prime Minister Keir Starmer meets police officers to discuss operational planning in London on May 15, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Failed reset: Critics called Starmer’s make-or-break speech after the election losses “utterly inadequate,” and later policy proposals were largely overshadowed by the leadership dispute.</li><li>Union pressure: Labour’s affiliated unions also called on Starmer to quit, widening the rebellion beyond MPs and ministers.</li><li>Rayner factor: Angela Rayner said she had resolved the tax issue that forced her from the Cabinet in 2025, removing one obstacle to a possible leadership bid.</li><li>Makerfield risk: Labour held Makerfield in 2024 with a 5,399-vote majority over Reform UK, but recent local results in the constituency showed Reform winning every council ward.</li><li>MP arithmetic: More than 80 Labour MPs urged Starmer to quit, while more than 100 Labour lawmakers called for him to stay, leaving rebels without clear parliamentary dominance by May 15.</li></ul><blockquote>Where we need vision, we have a vacuum. Where we need direction, we have drift. - Wes Streeting</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Keir Starmer: Starmer said he regretted Streeting’s resignation and said Labour figures had a responsibility to meet the political moment, while his allies said he intended to remain in office unless formally challenged. (<a href='https://tribune.com.pk/story/2608214/uk-minister-quits-calls-for-leadership-contest'>Tribune</a>)</li><li>Josh Simons: The Labour MP for Makerfield stressed the personal cost of leaving a seat he called his family’s home, saying doctors at Wigan Infirmary had recently saved his newborn son’s life, but argued that he had chosen to act rather than defend the status quo. (<a href='https://www.huffingtonpost.co.uk/entry/labour-mp-quits-seat-to-let-andy-burnham-make-mp-comeback-and-launch-labour-leadership-bid_uk_6a05e5afe4b0def65bfc5a8c'>HuffPost UK</a>)</li><li>Regional Labour MP: One Labour MP in the region told Politico that Reform’s recent “Vote Reform. Get Starmer Out” message would be harder to use against Burnham because Burnham’s candidacy is being presented as a route to replacing Starmer. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/labour-tries-unite-stop-farage-wreck-leadership-fight-starmer-crisis-uk/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>Tim Bale: The Queen Mary University of London politics professor said Labour appeared to have concluded that Starmer would have to be replaced by someone better able to connect with the public. (<a href='https://www.independent.com.mt/articles/2026-05-15/world-news/UK-Labour-government-faces-weeks-of-uncertainty-over-the-prime-minister-s-future-6736289757'>The Independent Malta</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/uk-government-faces-weeks-uncertainty-prime-ministers-future-132994036'>UK government faces weeks of uncertainty over the prime minister&#x27;s future</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/uk-politics-how-starmer-survives-as-farage-waits-in-wings/a-77170215'>UK politics: How Starmer survives as Farage waits in wings</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/uk-health-secretary-resigns-setting-up-potential-labour-leadership-challenge-to-starmer/article70981415.ece'>U.K. Health Secretary resigns, setting up potential Labour leadership challenge to Starmer</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/keir-starmer-uk-labour-leadership-turmoil-economy-pressures-pound-slump-stock-market/'>Starmer drama has UK markets reliving their Truss nightmare</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/05/15/nx-s1-5822492/u-k-prime-minister-keir-starmer-faces-challenges-from-his-own-party'>U.K. Prime Minister Keir Starmer faces challenges from his own party</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/05/15/uk-pm-starmer-s-rivals-make-cautious-moves_6753485_4.html'>UK PM Starmer&#x27;s rivals make cautious moves</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/Europe/2026/0515/uk-prime-minister-keir-starmer-andy-burnham-wes-streeting'>Another prime minister appears to be on his way out. Why is the UK so hard to govern?</a> - csmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-uk-government-prime-minister-starmer/'>U.K. government faces weeks of uncertainty as PM Starmer struggles to stay in power</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/05/15/2026/political-rivals-are-cl